{"SurveyEntry":{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","SurveyName":"Bayes BATS-post","SurveyDescription":null,"SurveyOwnerID":"UR_9udbooUzBxqTdLU","SurveyBrandID":"udenver","DivisionID":null,"SurveyLanguage":"EN","SurveyActiveResponseSet":"RS_0e27yoCzx1dh9ye","SurveyStatus":"Active","SurveyStartDate":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","SurveyExpirationDate":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","SurveyCreationDate":"2024-01-26 12:49:25","CreatorID":"UR_9udbooUzBxqTdLU","LastModified":"2024-03-14 08:08:35","LastAccessed":"0000-00-00 00:00:00","LastActivated":"2024-03-14 08:08:35","Deleted":null},"SurveyElements":[{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"BL","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Blocks","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":[{"Type":"Default","Description":"Questions","ID":"BL_cT2rCKyo0jQDeXI","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID2"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID4"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID5"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID6"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID7"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID8"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID9"}],"Options":{"BlockLocking":"false","RandomizeQuestions":"false","BlockVisibility":"Expanded"}},{"Type":"Trash","Description":"Trash \/ Unused Questions","ID":"BL_0HRGW5gXukYP3Ui","BlockElements":[{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID12"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID10"},{"Type":"Question","QuestionID":"QID11"}]}]},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"FL","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Flow","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"Flow":[{"ID":"BL_cT2rCKyo0jQDeXI","Type":"Block","FlowID":"FL_2"}],"Properties":{"Count":4},"FlowID":"FL_1","Type":"Root"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"PL","PrimaryAttribute":"Preview Link","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"PreviewType":"Brand","PreviewID":"3256e956-34d2-4194-97c3-19e4df8f56e8"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"PROJ","PrimaryAttribute":"CORE","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":"1.1.0","Payload":{"ProjectCategory":"CORE","SchemaVersion":"1.1.0"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"QC","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Question Count","SecondaryAttribute":"12","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"RS","PrimaryAttribute":"RS_0e27yoCzx1dh9ye","SecondaryAttribute":"Default Response Set","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":null},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SCO","PrimaryAttribute":"Scoring","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"ScoringCategories":[],"ScoringCategoryGroups":[],"ScoringSummaryCategory":null,"ScoringSummaryAfterQuestions":0,"ScoringSummaryAfterSurvey":0,"DefaultScoringCategory":null,"AutoScoringCategory":null}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SO","PrimaryAttribute":"Survey Options","SecondaryAttribute":null,"TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"BackButton":"false","SaveAndContinue":"true","SurveyProtection":"PublicSurvey","BallotBoxStuffingPrevention":"false","NoIndex":"Yes","SecureResponseFiles":"true","SurveyExpiration":"None","SurveyTermination":"DefaultMessage","Header":"","Footer":"","ProgressBarDisplay":"None","PartialData":"+1 week","ValidationMessage":"","PreviousButton":"","NextButton":"","SurveyTitle":"Qualtrics Survey | Qualtrics Experience Management","SkinLibrary":"udenver","SkinType":"templated","Skin":{"brandingId":"6793088960","templateId":"*base","overrides":null},"NewScoring":1,"SurveyMetaDescription":"The most powerful, simple and trusted way to gather experience data. Start your journey to experience management and try a free account today.","SurveyName":"Bayes BATS-post","ProtectSelectionIds":true}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Differen...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Different Statistical Paradigms: Comparing Frequentist and Bayesian Approaches.\" The study is a normal lesson plan that will take place during our scheduled class time as part of this course.<br><br>The purpose of this study is to understand the impact of implementing various statistical approaches in disciplines outside of statistics. This activity is focused on a real dataset, to which you will apply a guided statistical analysis. You will follow a structured process to analyze the dataset and interpret the results in small groups. You will randomly be assigned to one of two different groups that use different statistical approaches to come to your own conclusions about the dataset at hand. Through a final full-group discussion, we will compare the two approaches. This research study will be used to better understand 1) attitude changes after an active learning activity and 2) assess the impacts of the activity among students in disciplines outside of statistics. The answers collected during the activity will be used to publish academic papers that will be presented at conferences, with the hope of advancing scholarship on analytics education practices.<br><br>If you decide to participate, please understand your participation in completing the two surveys is voluntary and you have the right to withdraw and discontinue participation at any time without penalty or loss of benefits to which you are otherwise entitled. The alternative is not to participate in the surveys. Your completion of this survey indicates your consent to participate in this research study. No benefits accrue to you for answering the survey, but your responses will be used to understand your attitudes about statistics. Any discomfort or inconvenience to you are related to the difficulty in the activity content, but they are not expected to be any greater that anything you encounter in everyday life. Data will be collected using the Internet; no guarantees can be made regarding the interception of data sent via the Internet by any third party. Confidentiality will be maintained to the degree permitted by the technology used.<br><br>Your decision whether or not to participate will not affect your future relationships with me. If you decide to participate, you are free to stop at any time; you may also skip questions if you don't want to answer them or you may choose not to return the survey. Please feel free to ask questions regarding this study. You may contact me if you have additional questions at stefani.langehennig@du.edu.<br><br>If you are not satisfied with how this study is being conducted, or if you have any concerns, complaints, or general questions about the research or your rights as a participant, please contact the University of Denver (DU) Institutional Review Board to speak to someone independent of the research team at IRBAdmin@du.edu.<br><br>Anonymous data from this study may be shared with the research community at large to advance science and health. We will remove or code any personal information that could identify you before files are shared with other researchers to ensure that, by current scientific standards and known methods, no one will be able to identify you from the information we share. Despite these measures, we cannot guarantee anonymity of your personal data.<br><br>By clicking the link below, I confirm that I have read this form and decided that I will participate in the project described above. Its general purposes, the particulars of involvement, and possible risks and inconveniences have been explained to my satisfaction. I understand that I can discontinue participation at any time. My consent also indicates that I am at least 18 years of age.<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Description","QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Differen...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID10"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID11","SecondaryAttribute":"Click to write the question text","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Click to write the question text","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q9","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Click to write the question text","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 1"},"2":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 2"},"3":{"Display":"Click to write Choice 3"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2","3"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID11"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID12","SecondaryAttribute":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Differen...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Different Statistical Paradigms: Comparing Frequentist and Bayesian Approaches.\" The study is a normal lesson plan that will take place during our scheduled class time as part of this course.<br><br>The purpose of this study is to understand the impact of implementing various statistical approaches in disciplines outside of statistics. This activity is focused on a real dataset, to which you will apply a guided statistical analysis. You will follow a structured process to analyze the dataset and interpret the results in small groups. You will randomly be assigned to one of two different groups that use different statistical approaches to come to your own conclusions about the dataset at hand. Through a final full-group discussion, we will compare the two approaches. This research study will be used to better understand 1) attitude changes after an active learning activity and 2) assess the impacts of the activity among students in disciplines outside of statistics. The answers collected during the activity will be used to publish academic papers that will be presented at conferences, with the hope of advancing scholarship on analytics education practices.<br><br>If you decide to participate, please understand your participation in completing the two surveys is voluntary and you have the right to withdraw and discontinue participation at any time without penalty or loss of benefits to which you are otherwise entitled. The alternative is not to participate in the surveys. Your completion of this survey indicates your consent to participate in this research study. No benefits accrue to you for answering the survey, but your responses will be used to understand your attitudes about statistics. Any discomfort or inconvenience to you are related to the difficulty in the activity content, but they are not expected to be any greater that anything you encounter in everyday life. Data will be collected using the Internet; no guarantees can be made regarding the interception of data sent via the Internet by any third party. Confidentiality will be maintained to the degree permitted by the technology used.\r\n\r\nYour decision whether or not to participate will not affect your future relationships with me. If you decide to participate, you are free to stop at any time; you may also skip questions if you don't want to answer them or you may choose not to return the survey. Please feel free to ask questions regarding this study. You may contact me if you have additional questions at stefani.langehennig@du.edu.\r\n\r\nIf you are not satisfied with how this study is being conducted, or if you have any concerns, complaints, or general questions about the research or your rights as a participant, please contact the University of Denver (DU) Institutional Review Board to speak to someone independent of the research team at IRBAdmin@du.edu.\r\n\r\nAnonymous data from this study may be shared with the research community at large to advance science and health. We will remove or code any personal information that could identify you before files are shared with other researchers to ensure that, by current scientific standards and known methods, no one will be able to identify you from the information we share. Despite these measures, we cannot guarantee anonymity of your personal data.\r\n\r\nBy clicking the link below, I confirm that I have read this form and decided that I will participate in the project described above. Its general purposes, the particulars of involvement, and possible risks and inconveniences have been explained to my satisfaction. I understand that I can discontinue participation at any time. My consent also indicates that I am at least 18 years of age.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"SL","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Please read this carefully. It tells you about your rights in the study \"Introduction to Differen...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionID":"QID12"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID2","SecondaryAttribute":"To what degree do you (dis) agree with the following statement: There is no uncertainty in the resul","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"To what degree do you (dis) agree with the following statement: There is no uncertainty in the results of a statistical analysis.","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1-lickert","QuestionID":"QID2","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"SpecifyLabel","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidth":25,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"To what degree do you (dis) agree with the following statement: There is no uncertainty in the resul","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Before activity"},"2":{"Display":"After activity"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":6,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Strongly disagree"},"2":{"Display":"Somewhat disagree"},"3":{"Display":"Neither agree nor disagree"},"4":{"Display":"Somewhat agree"},"5":{"Display":"Strongly agree"}},"AnswerOrder":[1,2,3,4,5],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID4","SecondaryAttribute":"In 1-2 sentences, describe your reasoning for your answers to Q1 (just above).","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In 1-2 sentences, describe your reasoning for your answers to Q1 (just above).","DefaultChoices":false,"DataExportTag":"Q1-text","QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"ESTB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"In 1-2 sentences, describe your reasoning for your answers to Q1 (just above).","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionID":"QID4","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_e56duk8L2ejocuO","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID5","SecondaryAttribute":"To what degree do you (dis) agree with the following statement: The results of a statis